@node fat95_baked_into_Kickstart_ROM "fat95 baked into Kickstart ROM"
@{i}fat95 baked into Kickstart ROM@{ui}

v3.24+: cold-boot registration of @{fg shine}FAT\0@{fg text} .. @{fg shine}FAT\8@{fg text} (the DosType-byte
scheme) plus @{fg shine}464154FF@{fg text} (the device-name scheme): ten fat95 entries, all
sharing the same handler code (same @{fg shine}Loc@{fg text} ). ROM registration was broken
before fat95 3.22, so prior ROM builds still fall back to @{fg shine}L:fat95@{fg text} (RAM).

@{fg highlight}
   #: DosType (ascii) Version  Patch SegList  Loc   Name
  ----------------------------------------------------------
   1: 464154FF (FAT.)    00030018 0190  00E4CB14 [ROM]   fat95 3.24 (07.06.2026) [68020]
   2: 46415408 (FAT.)    00030018 0190  00E4CB14 [ROM]   fat95 3.24 (07.06.2026) [68020]
   3: 46415407 (FAT.)    00030018 0190  00E4CB14 [ROM]   fat95 3.24 (07.06.2026) [68020]
   4: 46415406 (FAT.)    00030018 0190  00E4CB14 [ROM]   fat95 3.24 (07.06.2026) [68020]
   5: 46415405 (FAT.)    00030018 0190  00E4CB14 [ROM]   fat95 3.24 (07.06.2026) [68020]
   6: 46415404 (FAT.)    00030018 0190  00E4CB14 [ROM]   fat95 3.24 (07.06.2026) [68020]
   7: 46415403 (FAT.)    00030018 0190  00E4CB14 [ROM]   fat95 3.24 (07.06.2026) [68020]
   8: 46415402 (FAT.)    00030018 0190  00E4CB14 [ROM]   fat95 3.24 (07.06.2026) [68020]
   9: 46415401 (FAT.)    00030018 0190  00E4CB14 [ROM]   fat95 3.24 (07.06.2026) [68020]
  10: 46415400 (FAT.)    00030018 0190  00E4CB14 [ROM]   fat95 3.24 (07.06.2026) [68020]
  11: 50445303 (PDS.)    00140000 0180  00E3DDD4 [ROM]   pfs3aio
  12: 50465303 (PFS.)    00140000 0180  00E3DDD4 [ROM]   pfs3aio
  13: 50445301 (PDS.)    00140000 0180  00E3DDD4 [ROM]   pfs3aio
  14: 50465301 (PFS.)    00140000 0180  00E3DDD4 [ROM]   pfs3aio
  15: 444F5307 (DOS.)    002F0004 0000  D2590000 [RAM]   filesysres 47.4 (16.1.2021)
  16: 444F5306 (DOS.)    002F0004 0000  D2C10000 [RAM]   filesysres 47.4 (16.1.2021)
  17: 444F5305 (DOS.)    002F0004 0000  D3290000 [RAM]   filesysres 47.4 (16.1.2021)
  18: 444F5304 (DOS.)    002F0004 0000  D3910000 [RAM]   filesysres 47.4 (16.1.2021)
  19: 444F5303 (DOS.)    002F0004 0000  D3F90000 [RAM]   filesysres 47.4 (16.1.2021)
  20: 444F5302 (DOS.)    002F0004 0000  D0F90000 [RAM]   filesysres 47.4 (16.1.2021)
  21: 444F5301 (DOS.)    002F0004 0000  00000000 [RAM]   filesysres 47.4 (16.1.2021)
  22: 554E4901 (UNI.)    00000000 0008  7C994110 [RAM]   filesysres 47.4 (16.1.2021)
  ----------------------------------------------------------
  Total: 23 entries in FileSystem.resource.
@{fg text}

@{b}Reading the fat95 entries@{ub}:
All ten fat95 entries above point to the same handler code (same @{fg shine}SegList@{fg text}
/ @{fg shine}Loc@{fg text} ). They differ only in DosType, which is how AmigaOS matches a
mountlist to a handler:
  * @{fg shine}46415400@{fg text} .. @{fg shine}46415408@{fg text} ( @{fg shine}FAT\0@{fg text} .. @{fg shine}FAT\8@{fg text} ) serve the @{b}DosType-byte@{ub} partition
    scheme: one entry per partition number you might mount.
  * @{fg shine}464154FF@{fg text} serves the @{b}device-name@{ub} scheme: a single entry that covers every
    partition, because the partition comes from the device name instead of the
    DosType.

So a setup that uses only the device-name scheme needs just the one
@{fg shine}464154FF@{fg text} entry, no matter how many partitions are mounted. See Partition
Selection (../README.md#partition-selection).

